    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>You are a Catholic priest in colonial-era Nigeria, called to a remote jungle village to assist a dying clergyman. </strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You set out with hunters, porters, a scout, cook, catechist, and healer. Each night by the campfire, one steps forward to confess. It's your sacred duty to listen, assign penance, and bring their soul to absolution\u2014or damnation.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >But as the journey progresses, the jungle thickens, the trail vanishes, and your crew begins to disappear, one by one.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Confession Gameplay</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Assign penance based on each confession using an in-game manual of prayers, fasting, and public acts. Confessions are procedurally generated for infinite replayability.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Folk Horror Narrative</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Inspired by <i>Heart of Darkness</i>,<i>\u00a0</i>and a true story my mother told me, the game unfolds through daily journal entries, encroaching dread, and a deadly final confrontation.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Immersive Setting</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Set in the thick jungles of 1885 southern Nigeria, experience a unique narrative told\u00a0 purely through text and sound design\u2014as your mind and companions unravel.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>You are a Catholic priest in colonial-era Nigeria, called to a remote jungle village to assist a dying clergyman. </strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You set out with hunters, porters, a scout, cook, catechist, and healer. Each night by the campfire, one steps forward to confess. It's your sacred duty to listen, assign penance, and bring their soul to absolution\u2014or damnation.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >But as the journey progresses, the jungle thickens, the trail vanishes, and your crew begins to disappear, one by one.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Confession Gameplay</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Assign penance based on each confession using an in-game manual of prayers, fasting, and public acts. Confessions are procedurally generated for infinite replayability.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Folk Horror Narrative</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Inspired by <i>Heart of Darkness</i>,<i>\u00a0</i>and a true story my mother told me, the game unfolds through daily journal entries, encroaching dread, and a deadly final confrontation.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Immersive Setting</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Set in the thick jungles of 1885 southern Nigeria, experience a unique narrative told\u00a0 purely through text and sound design\u2014as your mind and companions unravel.</p>",
    "short_description": "A European priest serving in West Africa journeys into the depths of the jungles to assist a dying brother. Each night, hear the confessions of a crew unraveling under dread, and assign the appropriate penance to absolve them. Confessions are procedurally generated for infinite replayability.",
